From: =?utf-8?b?T25kxZllaiBTdXLDvQ==?= <ondrej@sury.org>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:18:31 +0100
Subject: Adjust the openssl tests to OpenSSL 3.5

OpenSSL 3 provides RC2, RC4, Blowfish, MD4 and RIPEMD-160 only with the
legacy provider, allows TLS 1.0 and 1.1 only at security level 0, refuses
too small keys and formats some output differently. Backport of the test
changes made for OpenSSL 3.0 to 3.3 in PHP 8.1 to 8.3; the legacy ciphers
are probed, because PHP 5.6 lists them even when they cannot be used, and
the openssl_seal() and openssl_open() tests name their cipher, because
the default one is RC4 in PHP 5.6.
